[rvn-ple] Remap NEXTN's draft to Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP for a grafted RVN text checkpoint

rvn-w4a16 only. Two gaps, both named in patch 0057's note as the day an RVN
checkpoint ships MTP layers, and the graft stamp is that day:

  * configs/model_config.py rewrote the draft architecture to
    Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP only for architectures[0] ==
    Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration, so a grafted text checkpoint built its
    draft worker as a second 48-layer copy of the target. The new branch
    mirrors the multimodal one exactly -- deep-copy the shared hf_config,
    collapse to one full_attention layer, num_nextn_predict_layers = 1,
    which is what sizes the draft KV pool in
    model_executor/model_runner_components/layer_setup.py -- and it is gated
    on the graft stamp through is_rvn_text_mtp_graft, so an unstamped RVN
    text launch is untouched.

  * arg_groups/speculative_hook.py defaulted the draft path to the target
    path only for the listed (multimodal and DeepSeek-family) archs, leaving
    speculative_draft_model_path None for the text arch: the draft worker in
    managers/tp_worker.py then had no directory to read. The default now also
    fires for a grafted text checkpoint, restricted to the resolved "EAGLE"
    algorithm -- the name --speculative-algorithm NEXTN arrives as -- so
    EAGLE3/STANDALONE still require an explicit external draft path.

The default is placed above rvn_text_bundled_draft_unsupported() on purpose:
that gate refuses a bundled NEXTN draft precisely because no draft path was
given, and for a grafted candidate there is one. Patch 0057 itself is
unmodified: an unstamped RVN text config still reaches the refusal, and a
grafted one reaches it as the pass-through branch it was written to have.

No weight-name mapping is needed on the draft side, verified against
models/qwen3_5_mtp.py:308-321 -- Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP inherits
Qwen3_5ForCausalLMMTP.load_weights, which keeps only mtp-named tensors and
rewrites a top-level "mtp." to "model.", then "model.fc" to "fc" and
"model.pre_fc" to "pre_fc". Those are exactly the graft's names:
mtp.fc_embedding.weight and mtp.fc_hidden.weight land on the draft's
top-level fusion Linears, mtp.layers.0.* land on its single Qwen4ExpModel
layer, and the draft needs no PLE table because Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP
clears config.ple_layer_ids itself (models/qwen4_exp_mtp.py:46).

--- a/python/sglang/srt/configs/model_config.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/configs/model_config.py
@@ -103,6 +103,26 @@ def _hf_attr(config, name):
     return getattr(config, name, None)
 
 
+def is_rvn_text_mtp_graft(config) -> bool:
+    """Whether an RVN text checkpoint carries a grafted NEXTN draft head.
+
+    The graft tool copies another checkpoint's top-level ``mtp.*`` tensors into
+    the candidate directory and stamps ``rvn_mtp_graft`` (source, encoder
+    version, count) into its config.json next to ``mtp_num_hidden_layers: 1``,
+    so the draft layer sits inside the *target* directory the same way
+    ``model.mtp.*`` does for the multimodal Qwen4-Exp arch. The stamp rule
+    itself (count == 1, encoder_version == "rvn-mtp-graft-r1") is
+    ``rvn_mtp_graft_active``'s alone; this wrapper only adds the architecture
+    check, so a stamped config of some other arch can never be remapped. The
+    import is deferred: srt.models imports srt.configs.
+    """
+    if _hf_arch(config) != "Qwen4ExpForCausalLM":
+        return False
+    from sglang.srt.models.qwen4_exp_text_adapter import rvn_mtp_graft_active
+
+    return rvn_mtp_graft_active(config)
+
+
 def is_deepseek_dsa(config) -> bool:
     return (
         _hf_arch(config)
@@ -761,6 +781,25 @@ class ModelConfig:
             text_config.layer_types = ["full_attention"]
             text_config.full_attention_interval = 1
 
+        if is_draft_model and is_rvn_text_mtp_graft(self.hf_config):
+            # Grafted draft head on the *text* arch (patches 0058/0059): the
+            # candidate's own directory carries the source checkpoint's mtp.*
+            # tensors, so the draft is remapped and sized exactly as the
+            # multimodal case above. No weight-name mapping is needed:
+            # Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP inherits Qwen3_5ForCausalLMMTP.load_weights,
+            # which already rewrites top-level ``mtp.X`` to ``model.X`` (and
+            # ``mtp.fc``/``mtp.pre_fc`` to the draft's top-level fusion
+            # parameters), and it clears ple_layer_ids itself, so the draft
+            # never asks for the PLE n-gram table.
+            self.hf_config = copy.deepcopy(self.hf_config)
+            self.hf_text_config = get_hf_text_config(self.hf_config)
+            self.hf_config.architectures[0] = "Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP"
+            text_config = self.hf_text_config
+            text_config.num_nextn_predict_layers = 1
+            text_config.num_hidden_layers = 1
+            text_config.layer_types = ["full_attention"]
+            text_config.full_attention_interval = 1
+
         if is_draft_model and self.hf_config.architectures[0] == "Qwen3MoeForCausalLM":
             self.hf_config.architectures[0] = "Qwen3MoeForCausalLMMTP"
             self.hf_config.num_nextn_predict_layers = 1
--- a/python/sglang/srt/arg_groups/speculative_hook.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/arg_groups/speculative_hook.py
@@ -621,6 +621,31 @@ def _handle_eagle_family(server_args: ServerArgs) -> None:
 
     _disable_overlap_schedule_for_cpu(server_args)
 
+    # A grafted RVN text checkpoint (patches 0058/0059: the config carries the
+    # rvn_mtp_graft stamp) ships its NEXTN draft layer as top-level mtp.*
+    # tensors inside the target directory, so --speculative-draft-model-path
+    # defaults to the target path exactly as the arch list below does for the
+    # multimodal Qwen4-Exp. It has to happen *here*, above
+    # rvn_text_bundled_draft_unsupported(): that gate refuses a bundled NEXTN
+    # draft precisely because no draft path was given, and for a grafted
+    # candidate there is one. EAGLE only, mirroring the gate's own predicate
+    # (NEXTN has already resolved to EAGLE): EAGLE3/STANDALONE still require an
+    # explicit external draft path, and an unstamped RVN text config still gets
+    # the refusal, so nothing about a non-grafted launch changes.
+    if (
+        server_args.speculative_algorithm == "EAGLE"
+        and server_args.speculative_draft_model_path is None
